Description: USB device information and driver finder for the desktop
 confusb watches the USB connections. The first time a device is plugged in
 it offers (with a notification, or a window, as configured) everything the
 system knows about it: descriptors, interfaces, kernel driver and modules,
 device nodes, power state, udev properties, the full lsusb output and, for
 storage drives, capacity and partitions. Known devices are not offered again,
 and storage drives are opened with the default application.
 .
 It also looks for the driver and the applications needed to use the device,
 using a built-in catalogue by USB class and manufacturer plus Debian and
 Flatpak packages and fwupd firmware support. It shows what is already
 installed and lets you install, open or try each application. For instance,
 with a smart card reader it detects that pcscd is missing and offers to
 install it.
 .
 The interface follows the system light or dark style and is available in the
 official languages of the European countries.
